of metabolism via CYP2D6 and greater levels of M1. Follow patients closely for increased risk of serious adverse events including seizures and sero…","n_labels":93,"source_section":"상호작용","terms":["fluoxetine"],"combo":false,"context":null},{"label_of":"fluoxetine","mentions":"tramadol","section":"경고·주의","excerpt":"…e Disorder; and fluoxetine in combination with olanzapine for the acute treatment of depressive episodes associated with Bipolar I Disorder. 5.2 Serotonin Syndrome Selective serotonin reuptake inhibitors (SSRIs), including fluoxetine, can precipitate serotonin syndrome, a potentially life-threatening condition. The risk is increased with concomitant use ofother serotonergic drugs (including triptans, tricyclic antidepressants, fentanyl, lithium, tramadol, tryptophan, meperidine, methadone, buspirone, amphetamines, and St. John’s Wort) and with drugs that impair metabolism of serotonin, i.e., MAOIs [see Contraindications (4) , Drug Interactions (7.1) ] . Serotonin syndrome can also occur when these drugs are used alone. Serotonin syndrome signs and symptoms may include mental status changes (e.g.,…","n_labels":162,"source_section":"경고·주의","terms":["tramadol"],"combo":false,"context":null}],"observed":[{"ko":"복통","organ":"gi","serious":false},{"ko":"빈혈","organ":"blood","serious":false},{"ko":"울혈성 심부전","organ":"heart","serious":true},{"ko":"혼돈","organ":"brain","serious":true},{"ko":"변비","organ":"gi","serious":false},{"ko":"경련","organ":"brain","serious":true},{"ko":"호흡곤란","organ":"lung","serious":false},{"ko":"QT 간격 연장","organ":"heart","serious":true},{"ko":"낙상","organ":"brain","serious":true},{"ko":"두통","organ":"brain","serious":false},{"ko":"고혈압","organ":"heart","serious":false},{"ko":"저혈당","organ":"systemic","serious":true},{"ko":"저나트륨혈증","organ":"kidney","serious":true},{"ko":"구역","organ":"gi","serious":false},{"ko":"췌장염","organ":"gi","serious":true},{"ko":"폐색전증","organ":"lung","serious":true},{"ko":"세로토닌 증후군","organ":"brain","serious":true},{"ko":"졸음·진정